<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/>
    <title>Complete Linux Learning Guide</title>

    <style>

        *{
            margin:0;
            padding:0;
            box-sizing:border-box;
        }

        body{
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background:#f4f7fb;
            color:#222;
            line-height:1.8;
        }

        .header{
            background:linear-gradient(135deg,#2563eb,#1e3a8a);
            color:white;
            padding:60px 20px;
            text-align:center;
        }

        .header h1{
            font-size:48px;
            margin-bottom:15px;
        }

        .header p{
            font-size:20px;
        }

        .container{
            width:90%;
            max-width:1200px;
            margin:40px auto;
        }

        .card{
            background:white;
            padding:30px;
            margin-bottom:30px;
            border-radius:15px;
            box-shadow:0 5px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
            transition:0.3s;
        }

        .card:hover{
            transform:translateY(-5px);
        }

        h2{
            color:#2563eb;
            margin-bottom:20px;
            border-left:6px solid #2563eb;
            padding-left:12px;
        }

        h3{
            margin-top:25px;
            margin-bottom:15px;
            color:#111827;
        }

        p{
            margin-bottom:15px;
        }

        ul,ol{
            margin-left:25px;
            margin-bottom:20px;
        }

        li{
            margin-bottom:8px;
        }

        table{
            width:100%;
            border-collapse:collapse;
            margin-top:20px;
            margin-bottom:20px;
        }

        table th{
            background:#2563eb;
            color:white;
            padding:14px;
            text-align:left;
        }

        table td{
            border:1px solid #d1d5db;
            padding:12px;
        }

        table tr:nth-child(even){
            background:#f9fafb;
        }

        pre{
            background:#111827;
            color:#f9fafb;
            padding:20px;
            border-radius:10px;
            overflow-x:auto;
            margin-top:15px;
            margin-bottom:20px;
        }

        code{
            background:#e5e7eb;
            padding:3px 6px;
            border-radius:5px;
            color:#111827;
        }

        .highlight{
            color:#2563eb;
            font-weight:bold;
        }

        .info-box{
            background:#eff6ff;
            border-left:5px solid #2563eb;
            padding:20px;
            border-radius:10px;
            margin-top:20px;
        }

        .footer{
            background:#1e293b;
            color:white;
            text-align:center;
            padding:25px;
            margin-top:50px;
        }

        .badge{
            display:inline-block;
            background:#2563eb;
            color:white;
            padding:6px 14px;
            border-radius:30px;
            margin-right:10px;
            margin-top:10px;
        }

    </style>

</head>

<body>

    <!-- HEADER -->

    <div class="header">
        <h1>Linux Commands and Their Functions</h1>
        <p>Complete Beginner to Advanced Linux Learning Guide</p>

        <span class="badge">Linux</span>
        <span class="badge">DevOps</span>
        <span class="badge">Cloud</span>
        <span class="badge">Cybersecurity</span>
    </div>

    <div class="container">

        <!-- INTRODUCTION -->

        <div class="card">

            <h2>Introduction to Linux</h2>

            <p>
                Linux is a powerful open-source operating system used across the world.
                It is highly secure, fast, stable, and widely used in servers,
                cloud computing, DevOps, cybersecurity, networking, and software development.
            </p>

            <p>
                Linux was created by <span class="highlight">Linus Torvalds</span> in 1991.
                Since it is open-source, developers can freely customize and improve it.
            </p>

            <h3>Why Learn Linux?</h3>

            <ul>
                <li>Most servers in the world run Linux</li>
                <li>Essential skill for DevOps Engineers</li>
                <li>Important for Cloud Computing</li>
                <li>Widely used in Cybersecurity</li>
                <li>Supports scripting and automation</li>
                <li>Highly secure and stable</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="info-box">
                <strong>Did You Know?</strong><br>
                Android operating system is based on Linux Kernel.
            </div>

        </div>

        <!-- LINUX DISTRIBUTIONS -->

        <div class="card">

            <h2>Popular Linux Distributions</h2>

            <table>

                <tr>
                    <th>Distribution</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                    <th>Best For</th>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>Ubuntu</td>
                    <td>User-friendly Linux distribution</td>
                    <td>Beginners</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>CentOS</td>
                    <td>Enterprise Linux distribution</td>
                    <td>Servers</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>RHEL</td>
                    <td>Commercial enterprise Linux</td>
                    <td>Companies</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>Debian</td>
                    <td>Stable and secure Linux</td>
                    <td>Developers</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>Kali Linux</td>
                    <td>Cybersecurity focused Linux</td>
                    <td>Ethical Hackers</td>
                </tr>

            </table>

        </div>

        <!-- COMMAND SYNTAX -->

        <div class="card">

            <h2>Linux Command Syntax</h2>

<pre>
command [options] [arguments]
</pre>

            <h3>Example</h3>

<pre>
ls -l /home
</pre>

            <ul>
                <li><code>ls</code> → Command</li>
                <li><code>-l</code> → Option</li>
                <li><code>/home</code> → Argument</li>
            </ul>

        </div>

        <!-- NAVIGATION -->

        <div class="card">

            <h2>1. Navigation Commands</h2>

            <table>

                <tr>
                    <th>Command</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>pwd</code></td>
                    <td>Show current working directory</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>ls</code></td>
                    <td>List files and folders</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>ls -la</code></td>
                    <td>Show hidden files with details</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>cd folder</code></td>
                    <td>Move into folder</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>cd ..</code></td>
                    <td>Move back one directory</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>tree</code></td>
                    <td>Display directory structure</td>
                </tr>

            </table>

<pre>
pwd
ls -la
cd /var/log
</pre>

        </div>

        <!-- FILE MANAGEMENT -->

        <div class="card">

            <h2>2. File and Directory Commands</h2>

            <table>

                <tr>
                    <th>Command</th>
                    <th>Function</th>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>touch file.txt</code></td>
                    <td>Create empty file</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>mkdir folder</code></td>
                    <td>Create directory</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>cp source destination</code></td>
                    <td>Copy files</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>mv old new</code></td>
                    <td>Move/Rename file</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>rm file</code></td>
                    <td>Delete file</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>find</code></td>
                    <td>Search files</td>
                </tr>

            </table>

<pre>
touch notes.txt
mkdir projects
cp notes.txt backup.txt
mv backup.txt old.txt
</pre>

        </div>

        <!-- NETWORKING -->

        <div class="card">

            <h2>3. Networking Commands</h2>

            <table>

                <tr>
                    <th>Command</th>
                    <th>Purpose</th>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>ping</code></td>
                    <td>Check internet connection</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>ip a</code></td>
                    <td>Show IP address</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>curl</code></td>
                    <td>Transfer data from URL</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>wget</code></td>
                    <td>Download files</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>ssh</code></td>
                    <td>Remote login</td>
                </tr>

            </table>

<pre>
ping google.com
ip a
ssh user@server
</pre>

        </div>

        <!-- PROCESS MANAGEMENT -->

        <div class="card">

            <h2>4. Process Management</h2>

            <table>

                <tr>
                    <th>Command</th>
                    <th>Function</th>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>ps aux</code></td>
                    <td>Show running processes</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>top</code></td>
                    <td>Real-time system monitoring</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>kill PID</code></td>
                    <td>Stop process</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>jobs</code></td>
                    <td>Background jobs</td>
                </tr>

            </table>

<pre>
ps aux
top
kill 1234
</pre>

        </div>

        <!-- PERMISSIONS -->

        <div class="card">

            <h2>5. File Permissions</h2>

            <p>
                Linux uses permissions to control file access.
            </p>

            <table>

                <tr>
                    <th>Permission</th>
                    <th>Meaning</th>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>r</td>
                    <td>Read</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>w</td>
                    <td>Write</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>x</td>
                    <td>Execute</td>
                </tr>

            </table>

<pre>
chmod 777 file.txt
chmod +x script.sh
</pre>

        </div>

        <!-- PACKAGE MANAGEMENT -->

        <div class="card">

            <h2>6. Package Management</h2>

            <table>

                <tr>
                    <th>Command</th>
                    <th>Purpose</th>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>apt update</code></td>
                    <td>Update packages</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>apt install nginx</code></td>
                    <td>Install software</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><code>yum install httpd</code></td>
                    <td>Install package in RHEL/CentOS</td>
                </tr>

            </table>

        </div>

        <!-- DEVOPS -->

        <div class="card">

            <h2>7. Linux in DevOps</h2>

            <p>
                Linux plays a major role in DevOps because most CI/CD pipelines,
                cloud servers, Docker containers, and Kubernetes clusters run on Linux.
            </p>

            <h3>Linux Tools Used in DevOps</h3>

            <ul>
                <li>Docker</li>
                <li>Kubernetes</li>
                <li>Jenkins</li>
                <li>Ansible</li>
                <li>Terraform</li>
                <li>Git</li>
            </ul>

        </div>

        <!-- SUMMARY -->

        <div class="card">

            <h2>Summary</h2>

            <p>
                Linux is one of the most important technologies in modern IT.
                Learning Linux commands improves:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>System Administration Skills</li>
                <li>DevOps Knowledge</li>
                <li>Cloud Computing Skills</li>
                <li>Automation and Scripting</li>
                <li>Cybersecurity Knowledge</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="info-box">
                <strong>Final Note:</strong><br>
                Mastering Linux is the first step toward becoming a successful
                DevOps Engineer, Cloud Engineer, or System Administrator.
            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

    <!-- FOOTER -->

    <div class="footer">
        <h3>Linux Learning Website</h3>
        <p>Created for DevOps & Linux Beginners</p>
    </div>

</body>
</html>